# The ONE authoritative build-context ignore for every image built from the
# repo root (docker/Dockerfile + docker/viewer/Dockerfile, both targets).
# A Dockerfile-adjacent *.dockerignore would SHADOW this file entirely
# (docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context — "a Dockerfile-specific ignore-file
# takes precedence"), which is exactly the split that let the viewer context
# ship the whole ~200 MB .git while the server context dropped it; there is now
# only this file (issue #282 F1/D4).
#
# .git is EXCLUDED (owner directive 2026-07-24): it added ~200 MB to the
# context and invalidated the COPY layer on every commit/fetch
# (docs.docker.com/build/cache — a changed file busts its layer). Build
# provenance no longer reads .git at all: it flows through the OCI-standard
# REVISION build-arg (CI's metadata-action sets it; the driving scripts export
# it), which the server Dockerfile bridges into build.rs's compile env, and
# degrades to a version-only identity with SHA=unknown when absent.

# Build output — the whole point of this file (target/ once grew the context
# to 53 GB, 2026-07-24).
target/
**/target/
.git/

# Vendored spec text + generated site — not needed to compile; large.
docs/
docs-dist/
# The one docs/ file a build reads: app/ferroehr/build.rs derives the
# `OPTIONS /` conformance profile from it.
!docs/conformance/ferroehr/summary.md

# The vendored test corpora (~250 MB of clinical models). The builder stage
# compiles `-p ferroehr-server` only, so no test target — and nothing that
# reads these — is a build input. The comment above used to claim `docs/`
# covered the corpus; it never did.
corpus/
crates/openehr-adl/tests/corpus/

# The fuzz harnesses (#2813): their own NIGHTLY workspace, deliberately not a
# root-workspace member, so `-p ferroehr-server` never parses or compiles them
# — and fuzz/corpus alone is ~46 MB of seed inputs.
fuzz/

# The website sources + the locally generated site build output (#2813): pure
# prose/HTML, no crate reads them (verified: no include_str!/build.rs path
# reaches website/ or _site/).
website/
_site/

# Codegen INPUTS and reference grammars (#2813): the generated code is
# committed, the generator does not run in the image build, and every
# include_str! under crates/ that reaches a vendor/ path sits in tests/ (the
# openehr_sdk corpus in openehr-its/tests/it). openehr-lang's vendored .g4
# grammar set is reference text for the hand-written lexer, not a compile
# input (no build.rs, no include_str! names it).
crates/*/vendor/
tools/openehr-codegen/vendor/

# The vendored XSD bundles (#2813): read by the xml_xsd_validity test at
# RUNTIME, never by the lib compile. schemas/json/ STAYS — src/json.rs
# include_str!s openehr_rm_1.1.0_all.json into the lib (it is even in the
# crate's packaged `include` list).
crates/openehr-its/schemas/xml/

# Local terminology releases (#2813): the 681 MB SNOMED NL zip parked in the
# repo root for #2236 dominated the context; no tracked zip exists and no
# build input is an archive.
*.zip

# Agent worktrees (full duplicate build trees) and Node artifacts.
.claude/worktrees/
**/node_modules/

# CI, tooling, and editor dirs — never a compile input.
.github/
.githooks/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local env / secrets / coverage / logs.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.log
lcov.info
*.profraw
.sccache/
coverage/
.DS_Store
